      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, it is scientifically plausible that small social cues can influence group dynamics, as phenomena like the phenotypic freezing effect demonstrate how one individual's positive reaction can reroute collective stress. In your specific case, offering a calm comment may have served as a behavioral anchor, signaling to others that the situation was safe and reducing their baseline anxiety. While individual experiences like yours are subjective and not guaranteed, this highlights the real power of social contagion and leadership within tight-knit environments. Ultimately, tiny interactions can create ripples that temporarily stabilize an area's overall tension.",
